---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { commands, categories } from '../data/commands';
---

<DocsLayout title="Skills Reference" sectionLabel="How It Works" activeSlug="skills">

  <div class="panel-intro">
    <h2>Skills Reference</h2>
    <p>Every slash command maps to a <strong>skill</strong> &mdash; a <code>SKILL.md</code> file in the <code>skills/</code> directory. Skills range from zero-cost script-only operations (like <code>/idea</code> and <code>/status</code>) to complex multi-agent orchestrations (like <code>/new-project</code> and <code>/wrap</code>). Use the category filters to browse all {commands.length} skills.</p>
    <div class="key-points">
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What they are</strong>
          <p><code>SKILL.md</code> files with YAML frontmatter (name, description, arguments) and a markdown body defining the full workflow: preconditions, steps, error handling, and agent routing. Some skills are script-only (zero tokens), others spin up single or multiple agents.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What problem they solve</strong>
          <p>Skills turn complex multi-step workflows into single commands. Instead of writing a detailed prompt for "run tests, calculate score, generate docs, commit, and log session," you type <code>/wrap</code> and the skill definition handles every step, error path, and agent handoff.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="skills-filters" id="skills-filters">
    <button class="filter-pill active" data-cat="all">All</button>
    {categories.map((cat) => (
      <button class="filter-pill" data-cat={cat}>{cat}</button>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="skills-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table" id="skills-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Command</th>
          <th>Category</th>
          <th>Agent(s)</th>
          <th>Tier</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {commands.map((cmd) => (
          <tr data-cat={cmd.category}>
            <td><code>{cmd.name}{cmd.args ? ` ${cmd.args}` : ''}</code></td>
            <td><span class="cat-badge">{cmd.category}</span></td>
            <td>{cmd.agent}</td>
            <td>{cmd.tier}</td>
            <td>{cmd.purpose}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .skills-filters {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .filter-pill {
    padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 100px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.15s;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .filter-pill:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
    border-color: var(--color-accent-dim);
  }

  .filter-pill.active {
    background: var(--color-accent-bg);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-color: rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.2);
  }

  .skills-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  (function() {
    var pills = document.querySelectorAll('.filter-pill');
    var skillRows = document.querySelectorAll('#skills-table tbody tr');
    pills.forEach(function(pill) {
      pill.addEventListener('click', function() {
        pills.forEach(function(p) { p.classList.remove('active'); });
        pill.classList.add('active');
        var cat = pill.getAttribute('data-cat');
        skillRows.forEach(function(row) {
          var match = cat === 'all' || row.getAttribute('data-cat') === cat;
          row.style.display = match ? '' : 'none';
        });
      });
    });
  })();
</script>
